{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDED + LIVE VALIDATION.\n\nMerged to main as f2394af853 (Gerrit change 1722, LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, submitted and replicated). Worktree realigned.\n\nLive validation on epic 0e68-41eb-5782-4336 (outrageous-uncultured-wildebeast), run against the fix:\n\n- The target finding is GONE. norm_id n9d22a867f4a4d027 (\"the multi-project inbound fetch child ... does not address the three per-project enrichment passes\") was a `block` with `evidence: []` at priority 0.8889 in the immediately preceding round; with the fix in place it is absent from the finding set entirely. The ratchet is broken end-to-end in production, on the already-written sidecars, with no migration.\n- Recall still works where it should. Three findings came back with `recalled: true` carrying 4, 6 and 5 evidence items — grounded priors re-surfaced and re-verified against the current plan, which is the behaviour recall was built for.\n- The epic still BLOCKed at that point, on GENUINE findings rather than a replay: a G6 store-compat \"no window\" defect emitted FRESH with 3 evidence items, plus its independently corroborating recalled twin (4 evidence items), and three G3 advisories on parent AC2/AC7 coverage in child 1734. That is the intended shape — a real gap still blocks.\n\nHonest limit: `coverage[\"recall_suppressed\"]` is set in the Pass-1 coverage dict and unit-tested at the `prior_concerns` seam, but `build_payload` persists only a fixed subset of coverage keys, so the stamp is not visible in the sidecar (the existing `isf` key has the same gap). Widening what `build_payload` persists was out of scope.\n\nTest suites at the landed sha: integration 194 passed / 1 skipped; unit 12739 passed / 52 skipped with one failure in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_inbound_removal_confirmation_a4bd.py::test_pass_summary_reports_the_decline_count — the known order-dependent hammerkop flake, which passes in isolation and is in a package this change does not touch."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786619877040939001,"uuid":"7b163c64-90d2-454c-9ee6-099c53c7c86f"}